    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0051" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/705d: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-14T23:00:00-04:00">November 14,
                            1942—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1380. Your 1952, November 11, 8 p.m.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d48-f1"/> On August 7
                    the Under Secretary delivered to Ambassador Michels a memorandum<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d48-f2"/> containing a statement of the military assistance which
                    had been given and which could be given to the Government of Chile by the War
                    and Navy Departments of the United States. The list of items for future delivery
                    was to form the basis of a Lend-Lease Agreement to be signed after Chile had
                    broken relations with the Axis. These lists were immediately made available by
                    Ambassador Michels to his Foreign Office and to General Espinosa. At a later
                    date, Ambassador Michels expressed to the Under Secretary the very great
                    satisfaction <pb facs="0052" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/> of the Chilean Government
                    with the assistance represented by the lists of matériel.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to inform the appropriate Chilean authorities that the
                    matériel specified in these lists will be provided in accordance with the
                    conditions set forth therein. These conditions have been made known to the
                    Chilean authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
